{
  "id": "Compound::DB08932 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Macitentan is known to bind to Cyp2c19, which is a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in the metabolism of various xenobiotics. This binding leads to the participation of Cyp2c19 in the metabolism of specific substrates, including Tamoxifen and steroid hydroxylases. The subsequent participation of Cyp2c19 in the metabolism of these substrates results in the participation of Cyp3a4, a downstream enzyme in the metabolic pathway. The integrated evidence suggests that Macitentan exerts its effects through a mechanism involving the inhibition of Cyp2c19, which in turn influences the metabolism of substrates that are subsequently metabolized by Cyp3a4. The cumulative scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship between Macitentan and Cyp3a4, supported by the sequential involvement of Cyp2c19 in the metabolic pathways. The mechanism is biologically plausible and aligns with the known functions of these enzymes in drug metabolism.",
